  "next_action": "Do not train either one-stage directed sparse family. The monotone 44-to-88 gain and uniform per-layer recovery show that directed channel mixing is useful, while the remaining gap is representational. Test a nonlinear two-stage product of task-selected directed sparse mixers: 22 incoming coefficients per stage and target channel at the same 135,168-coordinate budget, plus 44 per stage as a 2x-capacity discriminator. Fit the second stage on the first-stage-transformed source, normalize the final BF16 c_fc endpoint to the deployed radius, and retain the singleton plus production-cproj hybrid gates. This directly tests whether two-hop channel paths close the reachability gap without a learned basis, LoRA, HyperConnection, or residual-topology change."
